Q.   What is multi stage docker build?
Ans : 
It’s a Docker build technique where you use multiple FROM statements in one Dockerfile to create separate stages.
One stage does the building. Another stage copies only the final build artifacts.
This way, you avoid keeping unnecessary files, dependencies, or tools in the final image, making it smaller and more secure.

✅ Why Use It?
Reduce image size.
Avoid leaking sensitive build tools or credentials.
Simplify your build process in a single Dockerfile.

✅ Example: Java Maven Multi-Stage Build

# Stage 1 - Build
FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17 AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY pom.xml .
COPY src ./src
RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests

# Stage 2 - Runtime
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/target/myapp.jar myapp.jar
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "myapp.jar"]
